<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:589e30ed1980e0563941d7992ad2e6c438c3cdb0299ea1c612069e1648a2bf57</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Vucic criticizes Kosovo war crimes verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5bb0988a9bcad99a33f884fec69615b3b87def40e64d0cd324f7dc4490b8914</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:47:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654--c1957e85b089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction of four former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has drawn sharply different reactions across the Balkans. Serbia has accused the court of failing to fully address crimes against Serbs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles, Earl Spencer clash over Diana death once again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07548539b68ca81f7aad2bfd7e7c2716717ad2f454b08b31a78dca43d54efb7c</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876--fe22dce63256.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Buckingham Palace has rejected criticism of King Charles III in a new book by the brother of his late wife, Princess Diana. Earl Charles Spencer has been a fierce critic of his former brother-in-law for decades.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Village votes to 'secede' in asylum center plan protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:936950d51c5b83ed9b095b1a4fbb4ad85bc0d0b82ab2717a876e48f6719be037</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T17:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826--f45e2135fb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Residents of Piddington, a tiny, remote village in Oxfordshire in England, have staged a "referendum" on leaving the UK. They are objecting to plans to open an asylum reception center at a disused military base nearby.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Canada and the EU deepen ties to counter Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf8160210780df49ba5cd8a0676c65b697711bdd86354f622fbbf134fb883bc3</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388--7ecef7e34741.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is known for standing up to US President Donald Trump. Now he wants to forge a "unique alliance" with Europe. But what could such a partnership look like?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Shock in Kosovo as Hague convicts former President Thaci</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c601f737482aab0a823a1d7dab2f810120de8c2da2fad8479e5f98a15354e643</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916--a5436d550055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction in The Hague of former President Hashim Thaci and three former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has caused consternation in Kosovo — both among political leaders and on the streets. DW reports from Pristina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British-American writer Bonnie Greer dies aged 77</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:112c5dd183cc380d046781f5c069ac3e8f10d06ee2476bbf202681b3c9345dab</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174--ca7cae1c3055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chicago-born playwright Bonnie Greer, who became a familiar face in British political discourse later in life, has died. Her husband David Hutchins announced news of Greer's death.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ddcb7eb0b7c0539b55a7141da2a5149fb4913183e29e53b02fc6078ebbcdedb</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e27127af6d6b029f346eed4454502ae8c61c14ccd9b892a4008a156efbc555fb</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f14ff007d2127ef5815098f65892b60cccc2dfea78902c1cf5f690156f060eb3</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why do authoritarian regimes target the LGBTQ+ community?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3d5e3e363106df26310cecc91723ab30922182ef18e17b0a27def4575689d2d</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831--8b4048f7a695.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-do-authoritarian-regimes-target-the-lgbtq-community/a-79276831?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A recent crackdown on the LGBTQ+ community in Turkey is symptomatic of a wider rights regression, according to experts. It's worse under authoritarian regimes, but why is it such a popular policy for these states?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598eb47ab6f8e96fde9edbeb636a43f4b7a5c861e7f1ce6a2dd2fbd0aa184239</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:290ec0976973816f341b5d8a55279a24e00327ef57d5c207496fef25a2b57ccb</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d21ad1b84f14ccde40662dc6c48237336a2ddc35d43e3055ff635c976351dd74</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:741340a4905e3aa5e12718b72d3d055a6d18c77edec71e26c1f1d5648099c6d2</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks halt to energy attacks by both Russia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5eeaa4cfac65cf2f1373d58e3cce61c76773fbba43e0fc2443d5bd0f5dc77966</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774--121a884cf5a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump, under fire for record US diesel prices, claims Russia and Ukraine have agreed to stop striking energy targets. Russia said nothing; Ukraine said "we expect specifics from our partners" on any such move.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urge unity after Russian strike on train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae5a063e9d0e3e980c2504ed78535d29f5b732948870726b1fc5861dc2ad88a8</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807--826cde282d81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's drone attack on a train near the Ukraine-Poland border has triggered EU calls to up support for Kyiv. Allies of Ukraine should show they "are not scared," said the bloc's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3c6f530add9c4d256a3ff3f84d8dac74d056e4f5f4a195c79b60e79a19947dd</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96745361842d955cd5f27a441ab731feef905804c6c7369f2174d157136086cb</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f707a4429a7fdd7fdb2d8000db62fe62dd0bf4e3cf6c305fbc517bde9461f99</id><updated>2026-09-17T19:46:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
